<title>USA: Drilex sees Q1 break-even EPS.</title>
<headline>Drilex sees Q1 break-even EPS.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Drilex International Inc, which is to be acquired by Baker Hughes Inc, said Thursday it would report revenues of $17 million for the first quarter, break-even net income per share, and cash flow per share of $0.28.</p>
<p>The figures will reflect delays in project starts and lower than expected revenues from Louisiana operations, the company said.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
